1
00:00:03,401 --> 00:00:07,453
Every kitchen starts as a job. Click New job.

2
00:00:07,453 --> 00:00:20,643
Give it a job number, a name and the customer.

3
00:00:20,643 --> 00:00:26,585
The job opens on its Cabinets tab. Notes travel with the job.

4
00:00:26,585 --> 00:00:29,822
This shop works in inches, so switch the units in the sidebar.

5
00:00:29,822 --> 00:00:36,383
Click Add cabinet and pick a cabinet from the library: first the sink base.

6
00:00:36,383 --> 00:00:42,208
Add a 3-drawer base for the drawer stack.

7
00:00:42,208 --> 00:00:47,806
Add a 2-door base...

8
00:00:47,806 --> 00:00:53,405
...and a 1-door base for the end of the run.

9
00:00:53,405 --> 00:00:59,122
Now the uppers: add a 2-door wall cabinet.

10
00:00:59,122 --> 00:01:02,651
Duplicate copies a cabinet with all its settings. Make a second wall cabinet.

11
00:01:02,651 --> 00:01:06,861
Each cabinet gets a number (B1, B2, W1...) used on the cut list and labels.

12
00:01:06,861 --> 00:01:09,465
Sizes show in inches now. Next, open a cabinet to set its size and details.
